    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Without a nonzero environment override, the tagged implementation divides both a one-GiB budget and one-quarter of the detected memory by `numCpus`, and chooses the smaller per-CPU cache size. Its calculation uses integer division through a memory-in-megabytes intermediate. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/third_party/tcmalloc/dist/tcmalloc/cpu_cache.cc",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:39942f911863f34d2fdad285e754d3e8f0b6062ff3b998912760b1c92e9cbff2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4340cbef1da210598cf6c5404c0d4cfb4b9da21fcde1de53703d3e8730a3d8c9",
            "ev:5eaff8162ebb6ce707df130735fac963d77ef6c6125bc0778d41ffd22bb94a08"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "8.0.16"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The tagged MongoDB parameter definitions allow `tcmallocMaxPerCPUCacheSize` and `tcmallocMaxTotalThreadCacheBytes` at startup and runtime. For the Google allocator build, the per-CPU property getter and setter call `tcmalloc::MallocExtension::GetMaxPerCpuCacheSize` and `tcmalloc::MallocExtension::SetMaxPerCpuCacheSize`. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_parameters.idl",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:532a0e42608917e67526db5456caaa320e222b98ca61944679134bc6db87783c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:99798cb61b39ee999eef4192bc9e263c67f49a87e75a820a6d849d898348629a",
            "ev:dc177fcce200526fef53a6752397f35086488c6930c7fc23b3858bede60c2b90"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "8.0.16"
          },
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_set_parameter.cpp"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the legacy gperftools allocator build, the tagged MongoDB initializer sets the total thread-cache default to the smaller of one GiB and one-eighth of the memory reported by `pi.getMemSizeMB()`. If `TCMALLOC_MAX_TOTAL_THREAD_CACHE_BYTES` exists in the environment, this initializer returns before setting that default. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_set_parameter.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7365c9d0d45cba3f27b362bbca2beaefc92db63e940c5f68089e3d18d09f4f22",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e7298ba54533d2e1302185aabc2c3a96393dbd2324997d5fe2b0187372d65e39"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "8.0.16"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Upstream TCMalloc documents `tcmalloc::MallocExtension::SetMaxPerCpuCacheSize` as a per-CPU control, so the application-wide cache total can be much larger. It contrasts this with `tcmalloc::MallocExtension::SetMaxTotalThreadCacheBytes`, which controls the total of all thread caches. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/google/tcmalloc/blob/master/docs/tuning.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:63953af0b7c0fd74fda538e7aa971927c7573ce4fa68840ac304a7b6f641b0f7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:68630c4462aee06d39ee8aec0b553326ffbcf451a7e514408870077cc34589ca",
            "ev:99798cb61b39ee999eef4192bc9e263c67f49a87e75a820a6d849d898348629a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_set_parameter.cpp"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Trisquare migration write-up reports that setting `MONGO_TCMALLOC_PER_CPU_CACHE_SIZE_BYTES=10485760` in its MongoDB containers caused `tcmalloc.cpu_free` to rise and slightly improved performance relative to its Bitnami baseline. This is an attributed result for that migration workload. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://trisquare.eu/blog/bitnami-mongo-migration",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2264a64c18136e08aa0b4760b5c86a33c5c7a0540c2e3be5679fbae0bfc9230e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:02c4d9c126e4b6cbd164134619944bfe50ac91357de5067ecac0746fe7628da3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Percona reports that its container-related allocator correction shipped in Percona Server for MongoDB version 8.0.16-5, made available on December 2, 2025. The release notes separately identify that version with the same release date. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-12)",
          "source": "https://www.percona.com/blog/a-failing-unit-test-a-mysterious-tcmalloc-misconfiguration-and-a-60-performance-gain-in-docker/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:13853622270f730f30b8362c90c693eed0d26e06db1087e8c72a67df9488db58",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15f70b9602a259bb7275b3bd1d224235dee49eb8f48143e46c84c44373b17839",
            "ev:6fd77f73532da4b02f9b0b9a5cffb0101aa614d0046c0077e464a0f21088292b"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://docs.percona.com/percona-server-for-mongodb/8.0/release_notes/8.0.16-5.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the tagged allocator implementation, `getMemorySizeLimitInBytes` checks `/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max` before `/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.limit_in_bytes`. For the first nonempty value it returns the smaller of system memory and the value parsed with `atoll`; if neither file yields a nonempty value, it returns system memory. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/third_party/tcmalloc/dist/tcmalloc/cpu_cache.cc",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:646fcc8e32583f5e710ca3020f82e1154b2b0325aa1a59f86440972125885b45",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0f40fdcb09d4f523795187bcf2f9ed85878041d8df3a486ca6700b569a7cb6fb",
            "ev:5eaff8162ebb6ce707df130735fac963d77ef6c6125bc0778d41ffd22bb94a08"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "8.0.16"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "In the tagged MongoDB handlers, `tcmallocAggressiveMemoryDecommit` is applied only in the legacy gperftools allocator build. Outside that build, the setter warns that the setting has no effect and returns `Status::OK()`. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_set_parameter.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7442fdfcde09297c56f59145df597820965522fc026116c9d1f3698849ebad23",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3102ff98e2a51214089a8ac34aab7472f11701b2cf04a21cc357a4bcaf24e23e"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "8.0.16"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The inspected MongoDB 8.0.16 server handlers use separate BSON and string validation paths. `validateTCMallocValue` requires a numeric BSON type and assigns an `unsigned long long` cast of the element's numeric conversion to `valueULL`. It rejects a value above `maxOkValue`: the minimum of the unsigned casts of `std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max()` and `std::numeric_limits<long long>::max()`. It reports an allowed range from zero through `maxOkValue`; converted zero is forwarded without the environment fallback. If the element's conversion produces a negative signed result, the unsigned cast exceeds that cap and is rejected. The string helper instead parses into `size_t` with `NumberParser{}(str, &value)`, returns a non-OK parser status, or forwards a successful value; this file does not define that parser's complete accepted syntax, coercion or overflow rules. The per-CPU parameter selects these helpers only for `MONGO_CONFIG_TCMALLOC_GOOGLE`, and the total-thread parameter only for `MONGO_CONFIG_TCMALLOC_GPERF`; other build branches warn of no effect and return OK. The property writer skips its allocator call under `RUNNING_ON_VALGRIND`. These inspected 8.0.16 handler paths do not establish interchangeable accepted inputs across entry points, and the finite allocator-file comparison does not establish 8.0.17 handler equivalence. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.16/src/mongo/util/tcmalloc_set_parameter.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fcd70d1d8b836fde55bbf741a80be3a63dca858e872ceb49a3a6a53deb6ca55a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0441ddc95c397784b98befe8baa0fb0b75b7cbb6d8e73686983d5ecf50251421",
